    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is rejected with a 400.\n\n**Change:** Added a `validateRegistrationDate` check to `ValidateOwnerFields.java` (the first step in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline), which already performs field validation and throws the checked `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` \u2014 mapped to a **400** by its existing escalation handler.\n\nThe check:\n- Reads the optional `registrationDate` from the request DTO.\n- If supplied and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, adds `\"registrationDate\"` to the error list, producing a 400 with the field named in the `errors` array.\n- Leaves the absent/valid case untouched, so `BuildOwner` still defaults an omitted date to the server's current date.\n\nThis fits the project conventions (validation consolidated in the `Validate` step, reusing the existing 400 escalation rather than adding a new exception/handler). The new `errorRejectsFutureDate` acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
